@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Native NoUpdate and unchanged-model next task
+
+This development bridge implements the existing no-change path in
+[`SELF_ITERATION_EXECUTION.md`](../../docs/readiness/SELF_ITERATION_EXECUTION.md)
+and preserves the owner separation in
+[`END_TO_END_LEARNING_SEQUENCE.md`](../../docs/lane-e/END_TO_END_LEARNING_SEQUENCE.md).
+It is not a second execution plan or production activation instruction.
+
+`LearningIterationHandleV1::submit_no_update` returns an opaque terminal owner
+result. The original learning snapshot remains `NoUpdate`; the bridge never
+creates a candidate `NextUse` receipt or a model improvement. The result has no
+deserializer or public constructor. The learning host still owns authenticated
+checkpoint restore and durable checkpoint commits through its existing ports.
+
+The next task requires the actual old generation journal, a freshly verified
+CURRENT selection and the existing Control / FinalUse same-model owner. The
+following mappings must already exist; an absent or different mapping rejects
+before the native prepare operation:
+
+| Learning owner material | Native generation owner material |
+| --- | --- |
+| Complete selected compatibility bundle digest | Selected manifest bundle digest |
+| Selected artifact digest | CURRENT-verified canonical manifest payload digest |
+| Completed task receipt | Atomic old generation observation digest |
+| Agent, cell and source run | Old guarded journal scope |
+| Terminal learning journal head | Deterministic signed next-task operation identity |
+
+The target retains the complete native manifest and principal while advancing
+the generation / writer epoch to a fresh task and run. The original same-model
+owner still enforces old output acknowledgement and drain, current selection,
+fresh purpose-bound FinalUse, durable claim and publication, and recovery from
+the original operation. A different CURRENT payload cannot authorize old work.
+
+`LearningNoUpdateSameModelTaskV1::into_runtime` consumes the real sealed Ready
+owner and captures its actual handle. `LearningNoUpdateSameModelRuntimeV1::step`
+delegates the exact task step and then obtains the live atomic owner observation.
+Only a committed Advanced / Stopped step with a matching snapshot and no pending
+request produces `LearningNoUpdateSameModelUseV1`. Native uncertainty propagates
+as an error. Its stable use ID binds the learning head, signed native intent and
+step receipt, so acknowledgement, drain and restart cannot count the same step
+again. A task can contain several successful steps. Count tasks by the native
+target binding and task identity, not by counting distinct step use IDs. Neither
+count proves new external business demand. The receipt grants `DENY_ALL` authority.
+
+The serialized record is an audit observation, not a standalone cryptographic
+proof. An external adapter must verify the original terminal learning owner,
+Control / CURRENT / FinalUse records and generation journal. A use ID or a
+signed-grant digest alone cannot authorize payment, installation or adoption.
+
+The native composition tests use real Fleet/config/service paths, signed
+selection and FinalUse owners, file journals, output fsync, acknowledgement,
+drain and runtime shutdown/reopen while retaining the authority owners. Their
+trainer, in-memory learning checkpoint port and proposal
+worker are explicitly synthetic. They verify owner composition and rejection
+boundaries; they do not establish independent customers or evaluators, external
+funding, a production model installation, a complete cost measurement or net
+learning benefit. Those gates remain open until their actual owners provide
+auditable material and a prospective, frozen evaluation completes.
